messages:
sam_support: Customer escalated — POST requests intermittently hang and then we see duplicate deliveries when retries kick in. They say it started after upgrading to Node 20 and our TS SDK v1.4.0. Customer report: some webhook callbacks executed twice.

alex_eng: Can you paste the minimal repro they used? any SDK config (retry/backoff) or custom AbortController usage?

maria_devex: They sent a small snippet and logs. Reproduces reliably for them with undici 5.x + global AbortController reuse. Copied snippet below from customer: 

sam_support: ```ts
// simplified repro from customer
import fetch from 'undici';
const globalController = new AbortController(); // they reuse this across retries
async function send(data) {
  try {
    const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.example/v1/ingest', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(data),
      signal: globalController.signal,
      headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }
    });
    return await res.text();
  } catch (e) {
    // SDK-ish retry loop (pseudo)
    await backoff();
    return send(data); // retries reuse same signal
  }
}
```

lucy_infra: Interesting — reusing the same AbortSignal across a retry path can cause odd state where undici's internal dispatcher thinks the prior request is still tied to the signal. There's an undici race we saw before where a reused signal can be observed as aborted mid-retry and cause the client to start a fresh TCP stream while the old one still completes.

alex_eng: Customer logs show a 200 then duplicate POST delivered ~1s later. That matches a retry being issued while prior request was still finishing but the SDK considered it timed out. What Node/undici versions exactly?

sam_support: They gave: Node 20.6.0, undici 5.15.0, TS SDK @redwood/core 1.4.0, app running on AWS lambda (edge container). Retry config: maxAttempts=3, baseDelay=200ms, timeoutPerRequest=800ms.

maria_devex: Repro steps we followed locally: - create an endpoint that delays response 700–1200ms randomly - run the snippet above - observe duplicate deliveries ~20% of runs. Important: when we switched to creating a new AbortController per send() call it stopped duplicating.

lucy_infra: Mitigation: advise customers to avoid reusing AbortController signals across retries. Also set idempotency keys for POSTs to prevent double-exec on server side.

alex_eng: For the SDK fix: we should ensure our request wrapper constructs a fresh AbortController per attempt, or at least per user call (if user passes one, do not reuse for internal retries). We should also make sure our timeout logic doesn't call abort on a signal shared by user code.

maria_devex: Proposed short-term message to customer: 1) please upgrade to @redwood/core 1.4.1 (patch ETA below) or use new per-request controller pattern; 2) add idempotency-key header for POSTs; 3) pin undici to 5.14.x if using older SDK as temporary workaround.

sam_support: Customer asked if this is a billing/charge risk — yes, if backend is not idempotent they may incur duplicate side-effects. They want a patch ASAP.

alex_eng: I opened ticket INFR-2187 and assigned to eng-runtime. Link: https://redwood.atlassian.net/browse/INFR-2187 — note: include reproducer in the ticket.

lucy_infra: Quick triage notes: - root cause likely undici/AbortSignal reuse race + our retry orchestration calling send() again while previous socket still draining - observed on Node 20+ with undici 5.15+ - reproducible with deterministic delay endpoint.

maria_devex: Work plan: a) hotfix SDK: ensure per-attempt AbortController and don't reuse user-supplied signal for internal timeouts; b) add a warning in docs about reusing AbortController across retries; c) add unit tests that simulate delayed responses + mock undici behavior; d) outreach to customers who reported duplicates; e) prepare patch release 1.4.1 with changelog.

sam_support: Customer appreciated the quick response. They asked for a short mitigation snippet to apply now. We gave: 

sam_support: ```ts
// mitigation — new controller per call + idempotency header
import fetch from 'undici';
async function safeSend(data) {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.example/v1/ingest', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify(data),
    signal: controller.signal,
    headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'idempotency-key': uuid() }
  });
  return res.text();
}
```

alex_eng: Also add this note: if you pass a signal into the SDK call, we will now clone it semantics-wise and not call abort on the original for our internal timeout (this will be in 1.4.1).

deploy-bot: Started release pipeline for v1.4.1-hotfix (INFR-2187) — build queued.

lucy_infra: Follow-up: we should evaluate if undici has a fix upstream or if we need to add backpressure/delay jitter to avoid overlapping socket drains. I'll file a minimal issue on undici repo with the repro.

maria_devex: Closing loop: assigned docs PR and support playbook update. I'll ping here when PR and patch published.

sam_support: Thanks, team — customer flagged high priority, will mark as escalated until 1.4.1 confirmed in prod. :thumbsup:
